    "narrative": "Today\u2019s landscape for the Austin Waves is limited as the majority of our offensive core\u2014including **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2014are off today, leaving us with a thin but tactical slate. Our primary play is **Liam Hicks** (55.93), who holds a strong \"Marginal-to-Strong\" profile despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status. Facing Shawn Armstrong, **Liam Hicks** benefits from a favorable 4.35 SP_xERA and a positive dynamic platoon split that pushes his base projection significantly. If **Liam Hicks** secures the clean-up spot as projected, his proximity to the heart of the order provides the best R/RBI floor on a day where high-ceiling options are absent.\n\nThe decision to slot in **Brayan Rocchio** (49.70) alongside **Liam Hicks** was a matter of necessity to ensure we are not leaving plate appearances on the table, though **Brayan Rocchio** remains a lower-tier play. His matchup against Nick Martinez is technically favorable given the 4.63 SP_xERA, but the expected #9 order slot acts as a significant drag on his scoring efficiency. The bench remains stagnant today due to the widespread team off-days, though we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL. With the rest of our roster\u2014including **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara**\u2014all inactive, our focus shifts to minimizing exposure and avoiding negative variances while waiting for the full squad to return to action tomorrow.",
